>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (First off, I am not saying astronomers are fussy or exceedingly difficult to buy for, let's be clear about that. What I am saying is that the astronomer that you love... wants to love your gift.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (For that to happen, you, my friends, need to ask them to give you a mini list of what they would prefer, because astronomy equipment and the gadgets that are attached to them can be extremely specific.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Once they give you a mini list, be sure they also tell you where they can be purchased.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( With all that in hand, you are good to buy and give.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This advice is to prevent you from purchasing extremely expensive items that they do not need or cannot use. So off you go. Make one of our PAS members happy with a nice gift.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
